.TH TRAIL 1 2026-10-17 "Peios trail 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
trail \- build and check Peios documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trail build
.RI [ options ] " [root]"
.br
.B trail serve
.RI [ options ] " [root]"
.br
.B trail lint
.RI [ options ] " [root]"
.br
.B trail help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trail
builds a static documentation site from a source tree containing
.BR trail.toml .
The root defaults to the working directory.
The binary contains its templates, styles, fonts, syntax definitions,
diagram renderer, and search engine.
.PP
Builds validate structure and links before publication. A successful build
removes output files it did not produce. Keep additional published files in
the source tree and name them in the passthrough configuration.
A failed build does not prune output, but it can have written some files;
publication is not an atomic directory replacement.
Unchanged output files retain their modification times.
.PP
Errors and warnings use stderr. Build and server progress use stdout.
Plugin diagnostics are replayed as supplied by the plugin, in dependency
order and then name order, including on cache hits.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build the site into the output directory.
Output defaults to root/dist. The page count counts HTML pages only.
.TP
.B serve
Build the site and serve it over local HTTP.
Watch source trees and declared plugin dependencies, including local merged
trees. Trees fetched from a repository are fetched once and not watched.
Debounce change bursts for 200 milliseconds, with a one-second limit.
Reconcile source contents every 30 seconds to detect missed events.
Ignore output paths and hidden path components.
A successful rebuild reloads connected browsers.
A failed initial build or rebuild prints a warning and keeps the server
running; output can contain partial writes from the failed build.
Missing pages return the built 404 page with HTTP status 404.
The server runs until interrupted or an operational server error occurs.
.TP
.B lint
Check the root's configured writing rules without building the site.
A missing lint table, invalid rule, or unreadable source is a failure.
Report findings on stderr, sorted by relative source path and position.
Line and column numbers start at one. End each finding with its rule name
in square brackets. Print error and warning totals after the findings.
Warnings alone do not fail the check.
.TP
.B help
Print help for Trail or for the named command.
.SH OPTIONS
Build options also apply to serve. Lint accepts the root and help/version
flags.
.TP
.BI "\-\-addr " address
Serve only. Set the listening IP address and port
(default: 127.0.0.1:8724). Port zero requests an available port.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-dangling\-links
Warn instead of failing on missing page, fragment, image, related-content,
and section-citation targets. Ambiguous references remain errors.
Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "\-\-cbpath " path
Also publish a second copy under a single path segment, with links rewritten
to stay in the copy. The segment cannot be empty, dot-leading, contain a
slash, or collide with a site path; it accepts ASCII letters, digits,
hyphens, underscores, and non-leading periods. The copy is excluded from the
sitemap and marked
noindex. No copy is written by default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass build-cache reads and writes, including retained source reuse during
every serve rebuild. Leave existing cache files in place.
Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "\-\-out " directory
Set output directory (default: root/dist).
Relative paths are relative to the process working directory.
Exclude the output directory from the source scan.
.TP
.B \-\-render\-llms\-full
Also write each print.md bundle as llms-full.txt.
Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Require nonempty article descriptions, except on link aliases, and warn
about authored site-absolute links. Link validation also runs without this
flag. Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print identical help text to stdout and exit successfully.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the program name and package version to stdout and exit successfully.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including help, version, and lint checks with warnings only.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure, build failure, or lint findings classified as errors.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error. No arguments prints help on stderr; other usage errors print
one diagnostic and a help pointer on stderr.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATH
Resolve configured plugin commands that do not contain a slash.
.PP
Plugins inherit the process environment. Environment changes invalidate
their cached output. Inputs such as network state and time require
\-\-no\-cache when they change because they cannot be fingerprinted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B trail.toml
Site and grouping configuration. See trail.toml(5).
.TP
.B root/.trail-cache/
Disposable cache, scoped to the Trail executable. Missing, damaged, or
unwritable entries cause recomputation. Successful builds remove unused
entries in that executable's cache. This directory is not published.
.TP
.B root/dist/
Default output. Contains HTML, Markdown mirrors, print bundles, search files,
static assets, discovery files, and explicitly passed-through files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build the site in the working directory with description checks:
.PP
.nf
trail build \-\-strict
.fi
.PP
Serve another source tree without using cached build results:
.PP
.nf
trail serve docs/learn \-\-no\-cache
.fi
.PP
Check a site's writing rules:
.PP
.nf
trail lint docs/learn
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trail.toml (5),
.BR trail-source (5),
.BR trail-frontmatter (5),
.BR trail-lint (5),
.BR trail-plugin (5)
.PP
Trail Learn: https://learn.peios.org/trail/
